# Construction Project Expense & Payment Tracker

*Product Requirements Document — for build in Lovable + Supabase*

> **Prepared for:** Development team — **Owner / decision maker:** Muhammad Wakeel — **Market:** Islamabad / Rawalpindi, Pakistan  \|  **Currency:** PKR  \|  **Timezone:** Asia/Karachi — **Stack:** Lovable (frontend) + Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Edge Functions; Storage used only for backup exports) — **Date:** 11 September 2026

---

## 1. Purpose

A private web application for a residential construction contracting business. For every house under construction it answers four questions at a glance:

1.  How much has the client paid me so far?
2.  How much have I spent on this house so far?
3.  What is the difference, and how much is the client still due to pay?
4.  What do I still owe to labour and vendors?

A site supervisor enters expenses daily from his phone. He must never see client payments, contract values, or profit. The owner sees everything, from any browser, through one link.

> **Design principle:** This is a money-reconciliation tool, not a project-management tool. No Gantt charts, no task boards, no material inventory in v1. Every screen should exist to answer one of the four questions above.

