## 3. Project types

Every project is one of three types. The type changes what the numbers mean, but not the structure of the app.

| Type                        | Meaning                                                                                                                              | What the contract value represents                                                        |
|-----------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Turnkey (fixed price)**   | We build the whole house — construction, material, finishing — for one agreed total. Example: Rs 1,20,00,000 for the complete house. | The full price quoted to the client. Expenses are our cost, so margin is real profit.     |
| **Labour only**             | Client buys and supplies the construction material. We charge only for labour and site work. Example: Rs 13,00,000 labour charge.    | The labour charge only. Expenses recorded are labour, wages, and any site costs we carry. |
| **Cost plus / supervision** | Client reimburses actual cost and pays an agreed percentage on top for supervision.                                                  | Calculated, not fixed: total expenses + agreed % (store the % on the project).            |

**Important:** expenses are tracked on **all three** types, including turnkey, so the owner can see the margin on fixed-price jobs. There is no type where expense tracking is switched off.

