## 5. The money logic

Implement these exactly. They are the whole point of the application.

#### Per project

```
total_received       = SUM(client_payments.amount)
total_expenses       = SUM(expenses.amount)                    -- paid and unpaid both
total_paid_out       = SUM(expenses.amount WHERE status = 'Paid')
outstanding_payables = SUM(expenses.amount WHERE status = 'Unpaid')

client_balance_due   = contract_value - total_received         -- "how much client still has to pay me"
cash_in_hand         = total_received - total_paid_out         -- "client money I am still holding"
net_position         = total_received - total_expenses         -- "the difference between both"

project_margin       = contract_value - total_expenses
margin_percent       = project_margin / contract_value * 100
budget_used_percent  = total_expenses / contract_value * 100

-- whose money, derived entirely from cash flow. Nothing is tagged by hand.
spent_from_client    = MIN(total_paid_out, total_received)
spent_from_own       = MAX(0, total_paid_out - total_received)
client_money_with_us = MAX(0, total_received - total_paid_out)
```
#### Site float (per user, per §4.7)

```
float_issued    = SUM(cash_issuances.amount WHERE recipient = user)
float_spent     = SUM(expenses.amount WHERE paid_via = 'site_float' AND created_by = user)
float_balance   = float_issued - float_spent                  -- "cash with you"

cash_with_staff = SUM(float_balance) across all users         -- admin panel
```
#### Cost-plus projects only

```
contract_value       = total_expenses * (1 + supervision_percent / 100)   -- recalculated, not stored
```
#### Company-wide (admin dashboard)

```
Sum each of the above across all projects with status = 'Active'.
Today's spend    = SUM(expenses.amount WHERE date = today, all projects)
This month spend = SUM(expenses.amount WHERE date within current month)
```
> **Whose money is a calculation, never a label.** When a client has not yet paid enough, the owner funds the site from his own pocket. `spent_from_own` answers "how much of my own money is sitting in this project right now" and falls straight out of money in versus money out. There is deliberately **no field anywhere** asking a user to tag an expense as client-funded or self-funded: such a tag would be set wrongly by whoever is in a hurry at a hardware shop, and would then produce a confident, wrong number. — — Critically: **own money spent is not a separate receivable.** The client already owes `client_balance_due` = contract value − received, and that figure already covers the work the owner funded himself. Do not add own-money spend on top of it, or the app will show the client owing far more than he does. Extra work outside the original scope is handled by **revising the contract value** (§4.6), which raises what the client owes — not by flagging individual expenses.

> **Display rules:** `budget_used_percent` renders as a progress bar — neutral below 80%, amber 80–100%, red above 100%. `client_balance_due` is the headline number on every project card. Negative `cash_in_hand` means the owner is funding the site from his own pocket — show it in red with the label "You are out of pocket".

