## 12. Row Level Security

RLS must be enabled on every table. Enforce access in the database, not only in the UI — a hidden field in the frontend is not security.

| Table                                     | Admin                                           | Site manager                                                                                                                                  |
|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| projects                                  | Full                                            | **No direct access.** Reads through a restricted view (see below).                                                                            |
| expenses                                  | Full                                            | SELECT where project is assigned to them. INSERT for assigned projects. UPDATE only rows they created, within the edit window. **No DELETE.** |
| client_payments                           | Full                                            | No access at all.                                                                                                                             |
| payment_milestones                        | Full                                            | No access at all.                                                                                                                             |
| contract_revisions                        | Full                                            | No access at all.                                                                                                                             |
| cash_issuances                            | Full — only an admin may create, edit or delete | SELECT rows where they are the recipient, so they can see their own float. No INSERT, UPDATE or DELETE.                                       |
| notification_settings, push_subscriptions | Full                                            | Own rows only.                                                                                                                                |
| vendors, expense_categories               | Full                                            | SELECT and INSERT. No UPDATE or DELETE.                                                                                                       |
| profiles                                  | Full                                            | SELECT own row only.                                                                                                                          |
| audit_log                                 | SELECT only                                     | No access.                                                                                                                                    |

> **Critical implementation note.** Postgres RLS is row-level, not column-level, so a site manager granted any SELECT on `projects` would be able to read `contract_value` through the API even if the UI hides it. Solve this with a dedicated view — `projects_for_site` exposing only `id, name, address, status` — grant the site manager role access to that view and nothing on the base table. The same applies to any aggregate function or RPC: none that a site manager can call may return contract value, payments, or margin.

**Do not use the Supabase service-role key in frontend code under any circumstances.** It bypasses RLS entirely. It belongs only in Edge Functions.

